
# 📊 Project Overview

This project leverages **Power BI** to create a comprehensive analytics dashboard for Indian restaurant data. The dashboard enables stakeholders to explore key metrics such as restaurant distribution, customer ratings, cuisine preferences, and cost analysis across major Indian cities.

Key datasets analyzed include:
- Restaurant ratings and customer votes
- Cuisine type popularity
- Geographic distribution across cities and localities
- Cost analysis by region

---

## 🎯 Objectives

- Develop an end-to-end Power BI report based on real-world restaurant data
- Identify key trends in customer preferences and dining habits
- Analyze regional variations in restaurant performance
- Provide actionable insights for business decision-making
- Create an interactive, user-friendly dashboard experience

---

## 🔍 Key Insights

### 🏆 Top Restaurants
| Restaurant | Sum of Ratings |
|------------|----------------|
| Kanti Sweets | 267 |
| Wow! Momo | 247 |
| Barbeque Nation | 212 |
| Taco Bell | 183 |

### 🏙️ City-wise Analysis
- **Delhi** leads with **223K votes** (28.39% of total)
- **Bangalore** follows with **102K votes** (12.97%)
- **Hyderabad** ranks third with **92K votes** (11.63%)

### 🍛 Cuisine Popularity
- **North Indian** cuisine dominates with **1163 total ratings**
- **Chinese** cuisine shows strong presence
- **Fast Food** and **Mughlai** cuisines also perform well

### 💰 Cost Insights
- **South Delhi** has the highest sum of cost (560K)
- **South Bangalore** follows (306K)
- **Gurgaon** ranks third (296K)

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

| Category | Tools |
|----------|-------|
| **Visualization** | Microsoft Power BI Desktop |
| **Data Modeling** | DAX (Data Analysis Expressions) |
| **Data Transformation** | Power Query |
| **Data Source** | Indian Restaurant Dataset (CSV) |

